<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lê Chiêu Thống</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1765">1765</a>–<a href="/years/1793">1793</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as Le Chieu Thong</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Lê Chiêu Thống was the last emperor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vietnam">Vietnam</a>'s Later Lê dynasty, reigning from 1786 to 1789. When the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tay-son-dynasty">Tây Sơn</a> overthrew the Trịnh lords and took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thang-long">Thăng Long</a>, he appealed to the Qing for help. A Qing army restored him briefly in 1788, but <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/quang-trung">Nguyễn Huệ</a> crushed it at Đống Đa in early 1789. Lê Chiêu Thống fled to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>, where he died in exile.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/le-chieu-thong.jpg" alt="Lê Chiêu Thống" width="320" height="202" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_King_of_Annam_at_Chengde_Mountain_Resort.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
